      "id": "LOCAL-101",
      "type": "loop-audit (negative finding)",
      "severity": "info",
      "description": "NO loops anywhere in NFTStaker. All reward math is O(1) masterchef-style (accRewardPerShare / rewardDebt). No array parameters, no iteration over users or token IDs. The single-active-ID design structurally avoids per-ID iteration."
    },
    {
      "id": "LOCAL-102",
      "type": "rounding (documented, by-design)",
      "severity": "info",
      "function": "_recomputeSchedule / _safePay / _updatePool",
      "description": "Floor rounding throughout (mulDiv floor on latestPrice, F, newRate, runway). _safePay has a documented <=1 wei/claim dust escape from rewardBudget when per-user pending floor-rounds above cumulative committedDebt. Asserted invariant balance == rewardBudget + committedDebt. These are local-arithmetic OK per design notes; correctness of the invariant under adversarial sequencing is an interaction concern (deferred)."
    },
    {
      "id": "LOCAL-103",
      "type": "external-dependency on caller-controllable view (defer)",
      "severity": "info",
      "function": "_recomputeSchedule",
      "line": 386,
      "description": "Reads nftMinter.configs(dispatcherIndex).price/growthBasisPoints and dispatcherHook.mintDebt() live. These feed rewardRate and windowEnd. Manipulability of those external reads (e.g. price ramp via minting, mintDebt swings) is cross-contract and deferred to interaction/econ analysis. Locally: totalStaked*latestPrice overflow bound argued in NatSpec (<=~1e27)."
    }
  ],

